Q: Setting the view encapsulation per css file A: <p>Angular doesn't support setting ViewEncapsulation per individual CSS file directly. Instead you can use wrapper compoenent.</p>
<p>create a seperate child component just for the select with ViewEncapsulation.None.  This isolates the encapsulation change to only what needs it:</p>
<pre><code>// select-panel.component.ts
import { Component, ViewEncapsulation } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-select-panel',
  template: `&lt;select [matSelect]=&quot;...&quot; panelClass=&quot;my-panel-class&quot;&gt;...&lt;/select&gt;`,
  styleUrls: ['./select-panel.component.css'],
  encapsulation: ViewEncapsulation.None  // Only this small component
})
export class SelectPanelComponent {}
</code></pre>
<p>Follow it with :</p>
<pre><code>/* select-panel.component.css */
.my-panel-class {
  /* Your dropdown styles here */
}
</code></pre>
<p>Then you can use this component in your main component (which keeps its default encapsulation).</p>
